# Production
dist/

# Local database
#
# prisma/dev.db WAS tracked, on the theory that shipping a seeded fixture makes the repo
# runnable immediately. It does the opposite. A binary that has to stay in lockstep with
# schema.prisma will drift the moment anyone runs `db push` without re-committing it, and
# a stale .db is far more confusing than a missing one: every page 500s with a "table does
# not exist" error that looks like a code bug.
#
# It is generated in two commands that the README already lists. Generated artefacts do
# not belong in version control.
prisma/dev.db
prisma/dev.db-journal
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Environment
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local

